From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:06:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dnsapi: Refuse resolver calls when Unix initialization failed.

DNSAPI remains loadable when its optional Unix resolver is missing. Its
numeric address and PE-only configuration paths still work, but the four
RESOLV_CALL operations currently dispatch through an uninitialized table.

Record readiness only after successful initialization with a nonzero
handle. Return ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED in the DNS_STATUS domain before any
unavailable backend call, preserving its output buffers and lengths.
A healthy backend receives the original operation and parameters and its
return value is unchanged. This supplies no DNS resolver, fallback,
server configuration or synthetic DNS answer.

The private boundary covers query, server-list and search-list calls;
DllMain still succeeds so numeric and other PE-only operations retain
their existing behavior. Keep the raw initialization status in the error
message instead of returning an NTSTATUS as a DNS_STATUS.

References:
 https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/windns/nf-windns-dnsquery_a
 https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/windns/nf-windns-dnsqueryconfig
 https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/system-error-codes--0-499-
---
diff --git a/dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h b/dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h
--- a/dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h
+++ b/dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h
@@ -130,4 +130,6 @@
     unix_funcs_count
 };
 
-#define RESOLV_CALL( func, params ) WINE_UNIX_CALL( unix_ ## func, params )
+DNS_STATUS dnsapi_resolv_call( enum unix_funcs func, void *params );
+
+#define RESOLV_CALL( func, params ) dnsapi_resolv_call( unix_ ## func, params )
diff --git a/dlls/dnsapi/main.c b/dlls/dnsapi/main.c
--- a/dlls/dnsapi/main.c
+++ b/dlls/dnsapi/main.c
@@ -32,16 +32,33 @@
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(dnsapi);
 
+static BOOL resolv_ready;
+
+/* DNSAPI also provides numeric-address and PE-only operations. Keep those
+ * usable when its optional resolver backend is unavailable, but never
+ * dispatch through an uninitialized Unix-call table. */
+DNS_STATUS dnsapi_resolv_call( enum unix_funcs func, void *params )
+{
+    if (!resolv_ready) return ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+    return WINE_UNIX_CALL( func, params );
+}
+
 BOOL WINAPI DllMain( HINSTANCE hinst, DWORD reason, LPVOID reserved )
 {
+    NTSTATUS status;
+
     TRACE( "(%p, %lu, %p)\n", hinst, reason, reserved );
 
     switch (reason)
     {
     case DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH:
         DisableThreadLibraryCalls( hinst );
-        if (__wine_init_unix_call())
-            ERR( "No libresolv support, expect problems\n" );
+        resolv_ready = FALSE;
+        status = __wine_init_unix_call();
+        resolv_ready = !status && __wine_unixlib_handle;
+        if (!resolv_ready)
+            ERR( "Resolver backend unavailable (status %#lx, handle %s)\n",
+                 status, wine_dbgstr_longlong(__wine_unixlib_handle) );
         break;
     case DLL_PROCESS_DETACH:
         break;
